{# geo_shapes — a low-opacity geometric accent OVERLAY for the breathing /
   atmospheric page (ST-31/ST-32). A quiet logo motif: a deterministic set of
   translucent circles, diagonal bars and triangles laid over the full-bleed
   atmospheric ground. Used edge-to-edge inside the breathing page's bleed block.

   Token-only by construction: this macro emits ONLY geometry (absolute
   position / size / rotation as inline styles — pure numbers, never colors).
   The fill / opacity / token colors live in the `c-geo` classes in
   styles/components.css, so the overlay stays brand-agnostic and the shapes are
   always low-opacity (never solid). The `--dark` modifier on a shape tints it
   toward the dark ink instead of the accent, so the motif reads over BOTH the
   light and the saturated patches of an atmospheric ground (contrast variety).

   Coordinates are ABSOLUTE LENGTHS in mm over the A4 sheet (210 × 297mm), NOT
   percentages: an absolutely-positioned child's `top:%` resolves against the
   containing block's HEIGHT, which is INDEFINITE here (the bleed block sizes by
   min-height, not an explicit height) — so `%` offsets collapse toward 0 and the
   shapes pile up at the top in WeasyPrint 68.1. mm offsets place each shape
   exactly, spread across the full page height. Negative offsets bleed a shape off
   the edge by design (the container clips with overflow:hidden).

   variant  1 | 2 | 3 — selects a shape ARRANGEMENT so the three breathing pages
            in a deck do not look identical (each page passes its own variant).
            Any other value falls through to variant 1's arrangement.

   Each shape entry: {kind, top, left, size, rot, tone} where
     kind  circle | bar | tri      (a ring, a thin diagonal bar, a triangle)
     top/left  mm offsets from the page top-left (may be negative to bleed off)
     size  shape size in mm (circle diameter / bar length; tri is border-sized)
     rot   rotation in degrees (bars/triangles)
     tone  '' (accent) | 'dark' (dark ink) — picks the token via a c- modifier
#}
{% macro geo_shapes(variant=1) -%}
{# Tone strategy: the DARK (ink) loops read reliably over BOTH the pale top AND
   the saturated lower field of an atmospheric ground, so they LEAD the motif and
   anchor the page top-to-bottom; the ACCENT loop is a single secondary highlight
   per page (it sits high, over the palest area, where the light accent reads).
   This keeps the motif legible for ANY ground brightness (a same-hue light accent
   would wash out over a saturated same-hue ground). A large ring anchors the
   lower third so the page is never top-heavy. The variants differ in lead shape. #}
{% set arrangements = {
  1: [
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': -26, 'left': 118, 'size': 124, 'rot': 0,   'tone': ''},
    {'kind': 'bar',    'top': 60,  'left': -26, 'size': 162, 'rot': 26,  'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'tri',    'top': 128, 'left': 152, 'size': 56,  'rot': 18,  'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': 166, 'left': 92,  'size': 152, 'rot': 0,   'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': 250, 'left': -36, 'size': 94,  'rot': 0,   'tone': 'dark'}
  ],
  2: [
    {'kind': 'tri',    'top': 26,  'left': 24,  'size': 64,  'rot': -16, 'tone': ''},
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': 14,  'left': 122, 'size': 104, 'rot': 0,   'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'bar',    'top': 152, 'left': 16,  'size': 172, 'rot': -24, 'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': 168, 'left': 108, 'size': 150, 'rot': 0,   'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'tri',    'top': 256, 'left': 44,  'size': 62,  'rot': 28,  'tone': 'dark'}
  ],
  3: [
    {'kind': 'bar',    'top': 18,  'left': 46,  'size': 170, 'rot': 58,  'tone': ''},
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': 40,  'left': -32, 'size': 100, 'rot': 0,   'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'circle', 'top': 146, 'left': 104, 'size': 140, 'rot': 0,   'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'tri',    'top': 220, 'left': 28,  'size': 64,  'rot': 20,  'tone': 'dark'},
    {'kind': 'bar',    'top': 264, 'left': 76,  'size': 140, 'rot': 8,   'tone': 'dark'}
  ]
} %}
{% set shapes = arrangements.get(variant, arrangements[1]) %}
<div class="c-geo" aria-hidden="true">
  {% for s in shapes %}
  {# size mapping per kind: circles are square (w==h); bars take their LENGTH from
     `size` (thin height is fixed in CSS); triangles draw from borders so they
     ignore w/h and only carry position + rotation. #}
  {%- if s.kind == 'circle' -%}
  {%- set geom = 'width:' ~ s.size ~ 'mm;height:' ~ s.size ~ 'mm;' -%}
  {%- elif s.kind == 'bar' -%}
  {%- set geom = 'width:' ~ s.size ~ 'mm;' -%}
  {%- else -%}
  {%- set geom = '' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  <span class="c-geo__shape c-geo__shape--{{ s.kind }}{% if s.tone == 'dark' %} c-geo__shape--dark{% endif %}"
        style="top:{{ s.top }}mm;left:{{ s.left }}mm;{{ geom }}transform:rotate({{ s.rot }}deg);"></span>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{%- endmacro %}
